---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import Card from '../components/Card.astro';
import { CATALOG } from '../lib/commerce';
---
<PageLayout
  title="Freeze-Drying Starter Checklist"
  description="A printable checklist for setting up, running, verifying, packaging, labeling, and storing your first home freeze-drying batches."
  path="/freeze-drying-starter-checklist"
  breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Starter Checklist', href: '/freeze-drying-starter-checklist' }]}
  width="wrap"
>
  <div class="checklist-page">
    <header class="checklist-hero">
      <span class="kicker">Free printable checklist</span>
      <h1>Your first freeze-drying batches, in order.</h1>
      <p class="lede">Use this beside the machine until the workflow becomes automatic. It focuses on the points that cause avoidable batch failures: prep, dryness verification, fast packaging, correct oxygen absorbers, heat sealing, and labeling.</p>
      <button class="btn btn-secondary print-button" type="button" onclick="window.print()">Print checklist</button>
    </header>

    <section class="checklist-grid" aria-label="Freeze-drying starter checklist">
      <article class="card checklist-card">
        <span class="step">01</span><h2>Before the batch</h2>
        <label><input type="checkbox" /> Machine is level, clean, and ready</label>
        <label><input type="checkbox" /> Vacuum pump / oil condition checked as applicable</label>
        <label><input type="checkbox" /> Food is prepared in reasonably even pieces</label>
        <label><input type="checkbox" /> Trays are not overloaded</label>
        <label><input type="checkbox" /> Batch name and starting weight are recorded</label>
      </article>

      <article class="card checklist-card">
        <span class="step">02</span><h2>When the cycle finishes</h2>
        <label><input type="checkbox" /> Check thickest / densest pieces, not only surface pieces</label>
        <label><input type="checkbox" /> Break or cut representative pieces to check the center</label>
        <label><input type="checkbox" /> Add dry time if any cool, soft, gummy, or damp center remains</label>
        <label><input type="checkbox" /> Do not package until the batch is fully dry</label>
      </article>

      <article class="card checklist-card">
        <span class="step">03</span><h2>Package immediately</h2>
        <label><input type="checkbox" /> Bags, absorbers, labels, and sealer are staged before opening the machine</label>
        <label><input type="checkbox" /> Choose a bag size that minimizes unnecessary headspace</label>
        <label><input type="checkbox" /> Add the appropriately sized oxygen absorber</label>
        <label><input type="checkbox" /> Heat seal the Mylar bag completely</label>
        <label><input type="checkbox" /> Inspect the entire seal for wrinkles, food, or gaps</label>
      </article>

      <article class="card checklist-card">
        <span class="step">04</span><h2>Label and store</h2>
        <label><input type="checkbox" /> Label food name</label>
        <label><input type="checkbox" /> Label batch / package date</label>
        <label><input type="checkbox" /> Add notes needed to repeat or improve the batch</label>
        <label><input type="checkbox" /> Store sealed packages away from heat, light, moisture, and pests</label>
        <label><input type="checkbox" /> Log package count and any failures</label>
      </article>
    </section>

    <aside class="notice checklist-note">
      <strong>Keep one rule above all the others:</strong> packaging cannot fix an under-dried batch. When you are uncertain, verify dryness before sealing food for storage.
    </aside>

    <section class="checklist-shop" aria-labelledby="checklist-shop-heading">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2 id="checklist-shop-heading">Packaging we sell</h2>
        <a class="btn-text" href="/shop">All packaging</a>
      </div>
      <div class="card-grid">
        {CATALOG.map((product) => (
          <Card
            href={product.detailsHref ?? '/shop'}
            title={product.title}
            dek={product.note}
            kicker={product.eyebrow}
            image={product.image}
            imageAlt={product.imageAlt}
            ratio="4/5"
            fit="contain"
            price={product.displayPrice}
            meta="Ships free · US"
          />
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="next-reading">
      <h2>Use the checklist with the full workflow.</h2>
      <p>The checklist is intentionally short. The complete guide explains why each stage matters and what to do when a batch does not behave normally.</p>
      <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/guides/complete-batch-workflow">Read the complete batch workflow</a>
    </section>
  </div>
</PageLayout>

<style>
  .checklist-page { padding-bottom: var(--s6); }
  .checklist-hero { max-width: 48rem; margin-bottom: var(--s4); }
  .print-button { margin-top: var(--s2); }

  .checklist-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: var(--s3); list-style: none; padding: 0; }
  @media (min-width: 760px) { .checklist-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); } }

  .checklist-card { padding: var(--s3); }
  .checklist-card h2 { margin: .25rem 0 var(--s2); font-size: var(--h3); }
  .step { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 1.1rem; color: var(--brand); }
  .checklist-card label {
    display: flex; gap: .65rem; align-items: flex-start;
    margin: .75rem 0; font-weight: 400; line-height: 1.45;
  }
  .checklist-card input { margin-top: .25rem; }

  .checklist-note { margin-top: var(--s3); }
  .checklist-shop { margin-top: var(--s6); }
  .next-reading { margin-top: var(--s6); max-width: var(--measure); }
  .next-reading p { color: var(--ink-soft); }

  @media print {
    .print-button, .checklist-shop, .next-reading, .checklist-note { display: none !important; }
    .checklist-page { padding: 0; }
    .checklist-grid { gap: .5rem; }
    .checklist-card { break-inside: avoid; }
  }
</style>
